Built on [pete-mcp-core](https://github.com/pete-builds/pete-mcp-core) — structured logging, healthcheck, transport wiring, and settings all come from the shared library.

## Install

```bash
python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"
```

## Run

```bash
# stdio (for Claude Desktop)
python -m {{ package_name }}.server

# streamable-http (for remote MCP clients)
MCP_TRANSPORT=streamable-http python -m {{ package_name }}.server
```

Or with Docker:

```bash
docker compose up --build
```

## Configure

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and edit. All variables are optional; sensible defaults live in [pete-mcp-core's settings](https://github.com/pete-builds/pete-mcp-core/blob/main/src/pete_mcp_core/settings.py).

For production HTTP deploys, set `MCP_AUTH_TOKEN` (generate with `openssl rand -hex 32`) and `MCP_AUTH_REQUIRED=true` to fail closed if the token is unset.

## Test

